*To: Hiring Manager*

// I am writing to express my interest in finance-related opportunities where I can contribute analytical rigor, business judgment, and technical execution. My background combines finance, data analysis, and operational problem-solving, and I am particularly interested in roles that value clear thinking, structured decision-making, and practical impact.

// Through academic, internship, and project experience, I have built a foundation in financial analysis, reporting, research, and data-driven decision support. I am comfortable working with spreadsheets, business intelligence tools, SQL, and Python to organize information, identify insights, and communicate findings clearly to stakeholders.

// I am most effective in environments that require ownership, attention to detail, and adaptability. Whether supporting financial planning, valuation, operations, or broader business analysis, I bring a disciplined approach to learning quickly, improving processes, and delivering reliable work in both independent and collaborative settings.

// I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience and skill set can support your team. Thank you for your time and consideration.

As a third-year Computer Science, Finance, and Statistics co-op student at the University of Waterloo, I am writing to express my strong interest in the Student, FCC Finance & Treasury Opportunities program at Fidelity Clearing Canada (FCC), with a particular focus on the Student, FCC Fund Treasury & Trading track. My background building quantitative factor models and complex 3-statement/DCF valuations as an Analyst at Guangdong Tiptop Asset Management directly provides me with the advanced Excel and financial modeling capabilities required to accurately compile trading reports, track portfolio performance, and forecast interest revenue. Furthermore, my extensive experience in data engineering—such as optimizing high-throughput data pipelines and automated workflows at the Treasury Board Secretariat—uniquely satisfies your team's preference for Python and SQL programming while proving my ability to identify and implement critical process automation improvements. Having successfully managed institutional risk and compliance during my software co-op at Manulife, I possess the meticulous attention to detail and analytical accuracy necessary to safely oversee credit limits, calculate daily liquidity needs, and manage high-stakes workflows within a regulated brokerage framework. I am excited to bring this powerful intersection of programming fluency and financial acumen to FCC's rapidly expanding clearing and custody business.
\ Sincerely, \
Jian Feng

